Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||05-13-2001||10:32 PM||||The Haynes manual aint telling the truth. Everything I try to do to my car is much harder than they let on.<P>It took me a good two hours to get the upper pivot bolt out of the alternator top. There was some kind of thick wax that wouldn't let it come out. And BTW it took an act of congress and another hour to get the alternator itself out of the car. Had to remove the mounting bracket and a brake line.<P>I'm getting afraid to go near it with a wrench.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||05-13-2001||10:36 PM||||hmm I just took of alternator bracket..than passenger side rear wheel and slid it out..thanks to the forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000002||voyagerspe||05-13-2001||11:45 PM||||on mine i also had to remove the alt. bracket. <BR>however i didnt have to take of the brake line instead i removed the pully on the altenator and it would then clear to be removed.  <BR>I agree the haynes manual lies<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ronnie||05-14-2001||12:15 AM||||I just changed mine Friday.I'll agree that the pivot bolt was a bit of a pain, but once I got it out, the alternator came thru the opening between the rear A arm and the frame. I had to jack the right side of the car up to get the needed space , but didn't take the wheel or the bracket off. Went right back in the same way. This was on the 2.8 V6, 88 model.<P>------------------<BR>'86GT/'88FORMULA/'88GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ronnies_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
